label Day4.impulse
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
# story challenge {"challenge_id":"Day4.challenge","playable_marker_id":"Day4.impulse.playable","end_marker_id":"Day4.impulse.end","board_profile_id":"week.canonical_solo","targets":{"never_started":"target.Day4.A","unfinished":"target.Day4.B","won":"target.Day4.C","lost":"target.Day4.D","perfect":"target.Day4.E"}}
\Below the edge of the bench, the pale satin ribbon around Lavinia's right ankle has come undone at the cross—tied in an unfamiliar square knot right over the tendon instead of folded flat behind the ankle bone where it belongs, one loose end trailing across the rosin. #id:line.Day4.impulse.001
\Kneeling on the floorboards in front of her, I gather both satin ends to untie the square knot. #id:line.Day4.impulse.002
\Just as my thumbs touch the cross, her heel slides half a step backward under the bench. #id:line.Day4.impulse.003
\The satin slips free. #id:line.Day4.impulse.004
\“Careful,” Lavinia says softly, watching the top of my head in the mirror. “You'll undo her knot.” #id:line.Day4.impulse.005
\My hands stop dead above the floorboards. #id:line.Day4.impulse.006
\In the wall-length glass behind the bench, Lavinia's eyes are fixed on my face—waiting to see what that sentence does to me. #id:line.Day4.impulse.007
\“You tied this yourself,” I say. #id:line.Day4.impulse.008
\“Did I?” #id:line.Day4.impulse.009
\“She doesn't know how a ballet ribbon crosses the joint.” #id:line.Day4.impulse.010
\“That's why it's a square knot,” Lavinia says smoothly, and as my fingers reach for her ankle a second time, she slides her heel another three inches back into the shadow beneath the bench—an awkward angle for her knee, baiting me to chase her foot under the seat. “Leave it. It holds well enough.” #id:line.Day4.impulse.011
\A square knot over the tendon. On her ankle. #id:line.Day4.impulse.012
\Hold the heel where it is. #id:line.Day4.impulse.013
