label Day4.A
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\Both hands rest flat on my knees without chasing the shoe under the bench. #id:line.Day4.A.001
\“Did you ask her to tie it, or did you leave the door unlatched so I'd think she did?” #id:line.Day4.A.002
\“That isn't your business.” #id:line.Day4.A.003
\“It will blister your tendon before Saturday.” #id:line.Day4.A.004
\A beat of silence. Then her right foot slides back out from under the bench and stops an inch from my knee. #id:line.Day4.A.005
\“Then tie it properly,” Lavinia says quietly. “Not too tight.” #id:line.Day4.A.006
\The square knot comes undone; the satin crosses once, tucks flat behind the ankle bone where it belongs, and smooths down. When I sit back on the bench beside her, she leans her shoulder against mine and opens the paperback again. #id:line.Day4.A.007
\“Read the rest of the page,” she says. #id:line.Day4.A.008
label Day4.A.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day5"}}
return

label Day4.B
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\Fingertips brush the leather heel under the bench, then open and draw back before closing around the arch. #id:line.Day4.B.001
\“If you want a square knot on your tendon, keep it.” #id:line.Day4.B.002
\In the mirror, Lavinia's chin tilts slightly. #id:line.Day4.B.003
\“Stopping there?” #id:line.Day4.B.004
\“The foot keeps moving.” #id:line.Day4.B.005
\“You weren't so patient with my waist.” #id:line.Day4.B.006
\Lavinia looks down at the crooked knot for three seconds, then bends, jerks the square knot undone with her own fingers, and reties it flat while her shoulder brushes my knee without telling me to leave. #id:line.Day4.B.007
label Day4.B.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day5"}}
return

label Day4.C
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\Instead of reaching into the shadow under the bench, my left palm stays open just above the floorboards where her shoe stood a moment ago. #id:line.Day4.C.001
\“You always tie a square knot when you're in a hurry,” I say quietly. “Nobody else touched your shoe.” #id:line.Day4.C.002
\“You sound very certain.” #id:line.Day4.C.003
\“She ties left-over-right on her welfare packages. That knot is right-over-left.” #id:line.Day4.C.004
\A short, reluctant breath leaves Lavinia's nose—half laugh, half sigh. Her heel slides forward out of the shadow and settles directly into my open palm. #id:line.Day4.C.005
\The leather at the back of the shoe is warm. #id:line.Day4.C.006
\“You're insufferable,” she mutters. #id:line.Day4.C.007
\The heel stays cradled in my left palm while my right hand undoes the square knot and folds the satin flat behind the bone. When I lift my head, our eyes meet in the mirror glass behind her shoulder, and she draws me up onto the bench beside her. #id:line.Day4.C.008
label Day4.C.next
# story marker {"kind":"scene.transition","payload":{"target_id":"target.Day5"}}
return

label Day4.D
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\Before her shoe can settle in the shadow under the bench, five fingers of my left hand lock around the arch and heel, draw her foot out from beneath the seat, and set her heel squarely on top of my own knee. #id:line.Day4.D.001
\In the mirror, Lavinia's breath catches; her fingers tighten on the edge of the wooden bench. #id:line.Day4.D.002
\“Let go.” #id:line.Day4.D.003
\“No.” #id:line.Day4.D.004
\Instead of easing the square knot open, my right hand catches the loose satin end and pulls it once, cleanly—stripping the square knot undone with a dry hiss of ribbon across her skin. #id:line.Day4.D.005
\“She ties her welfare string like that so a parcel won't come undone in the post,” I say quietly, my thumb pressing into the warm hollow below her outer ankle bone so she cannot slide her foot a fraction of an inch back. “Leave a square knot over your tendon for ten minutes and it will bruise the skin before you even reach the barre.” #id:line.Day4.D.006
\“It wasn't hurting me,” Lavinia whispers. #id:line.Day4.D.007
\“It was hurting my eyes.” #id:line.Day4.D.008
\My left palm stays wrapped around the warm tendon above her heel while my right hand crosses the pale satin twice—drawing the ribbon taut against her ankle, half a degree tighter than her usual rehearsal tension so she will feel the pressure of my fingers every time she points her foot—and tucks the flat fold behind the bone where no one else's hand can reach it without undoing mine. #id:line.Day4.D.009
\Then, without taking my left hand off her ankle, I rise and plant my right knee directly on the wooden bench between her knees—leaning in until her shoulders meet the cool surface of the wall-length mirror and my right palm presses flat over the damp waistband of her bodice where the four pencil marks were. #id:line.Day4.D.010
\Above my collar, Lavinia does not push my shoulder back. Instead, her right hand comes up and closes against the side of my neck—her fingers curling behind my ear, the pad of her thumb pressing hard into the pulse point just below my jaw. #id:line.Day4.D.011
\In the glass behind her cheek, a small pale circle of condensation forms from her breath. #id:line.Day4.D.012
\“You tied it too tight,” she whispers, her thumb pressing firmer into my throat. #id:line.Day4.D.013
\“You'll remember who tied it,” I whisper against the corner of her mouth, my fingers tightening on her waist. #id:line.Day4.D.014
\“And my ribs?” Her eyes blaze two inches from mine. “Are you going to keep your hand there until Friday so she sees it?” #id:line.Day4.D.015
\“If I have to.” #id:line.Day4.D.016
\For three full seconds neither of us moves in the mirror—my palm over the erased pencil marks at her waist, my other hand holding her ankle on the bench, her thumb pressed into the pulse at my throat. #id:line.Day4.D.017
# self-talk
\“Ești nebună,” she breathes in Romanian, and then in English\: “You're completely out of your mind.” #id:line.Day4.D.018
label Day4.D.thought
# story marker {"kind":"thought.options","payload":{"opportunity_id":"Day4.aftermath","options":[{"choice_id":"mirror","text":"Make her look in the mirror at whose hand is on her waist now.","target_id":"target.Day4.D.mirror"},{"choice_id":"friday","text":"Tell her I'll be here before the other door opens on Friday.","target_id":"target.Day4.D.friday"}],"pass_target_id":"target.Day4.D.default"}}
return

label Day4.D.default
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\Lavinia's thumb slides from my pulse to the back of my jaw, tilting my chin half an inch until her lower lip brushes the corner of mine—warm, sharp with honey from the pastille, neither of us calling it a kiss—before she drops her forehead hard against my collarbone while the mirror holds us both. #id:line.Day4.D.default.001
\“Sit down properly before someone walks past the door,” she whispers into my collar, her fingers still twisted in my lapel. #id:line.Day4.D.default.002
\When I slide off my knee onto the bench beside her, she does not let go of my hand; she pulls the open paperback across both our laps and sets her finger under the line where we stopped. #id:line.Day4.D.default.003
\“Go on,” she says softly, her shoulder pressed flush against mine. “Read.” #id:line.Day4.D.default.004
