label Day4.D.mirror
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\“Turn your head,” I murmur against her temple, keeping my palm warm over the damp wool at her waist. “Look in the glass.” #id:line.Day4.D.mirror.001
\Lavinia turns her cheek half an inch against the cool mirror until her eyes meet mine in the reflection behind us—where my coat blocks the rest of the room and only my hand on her ribs is visible. #id:line.Day4.D.mirror.002
\“Satisfied?” she whispers to the glass. #id:line.Day4.D.mirror.003
\“Her hand isn't there now.” #id:line.Day4.D.mirror.004
\Her thumb presses once more against my jaw before she pulls me down onto the bench beside her. #id:line.Day4.D.mirror.005
