label Day4.E
# story entry day=4
# art scene draft.reading.late
\Instead of reaching into the shadow under the bench, my left palm stays open just above the floorboards where her shoe stood a moment ago. #id:line.Day4.E.001
\“You always tie a square knot when you're in a hurry,” I say quietly. “Nobody else touched your shoe.” #id:line.Day4.E.002
\“You sound very certain.” #id:line.Day4.E.003
\“She ties left-over-right on her welfare packages. That knot is right-over-left.” #id:line.Day4.E.004
\A short, reluctant breath leaves Lavinia's nose—half laugh, half sigh. Her heel slides forward out of the shadow and settles directly into my open palm. #id:line.Day4.E.005
\The leather at the back of the shoe is warm. #id:line.Day4.E.006
\“You're insufferable,” she mutters. #id:line.Day4.E.007
\The heel stays cradled in my left palm while my right hand undoes the square knot and folds the satin flat behind the bone. When I lift my head, our eyes meet in the mirror glass behind her shoulder, and she draws me up onto the bench beside her. #id:line.Day4.E.008
\In the mirror\: the bench, the barre, the white flowers in the glass jar, and the narrow strip of corridor pane behind the door. #id:line.Day4.E.009
\The piano in the next studio stopped minutes ago. Not one shadow has crossed the frosted glass. #id:line.Day4.E.010
